From the cofactor relations $sum_i M_(i k) Delta_(i j) = (det matbold(M)) delta_(j k)$ and $sum_j M_(l j) Delta_(i j) = (det matbold(M)) delta_(l i)$, the adjugate satisfies
$
  tilde(matbold(M)) matbold(M) = matbold(M) tilde(matbold(M)) = (det matbold(M)) matbold(I).
$
Hence, if $det matbold(M) != 0$, then
$ matbold(M^(-1)) = (tilde(matbold(M)))/(det matbold(M)), $
which computes the inverse of a matrix using only determinants of smaller matrices.
